2026-07-24 - Item delete cleanup

Task: after an item (Entity) is deleted, clear its references from
Session/Character fields, since deleteEntity previously left dangling ids.

Files changed:
- utils/itemCleanup.js (new)
- controllers/commonController.js
- routes/commonRouter.js

--- utils/itemCleanup.js (new file) ---
import Session from '../schemas/sessionSchema.js'
import Character from '../schemas/characterSchema.js'

export async function clearDeletedItemReferences(itemId) {
    await Session.updateMany(
        { entities: itemId },
        { $pull: { entities: itemId } }
    )

    await Character.updateMany(
        { $or: [{ entities: itemId }, { 'loadouts.itemsIds': itemId }] },
        { $pull: { entities: itemId, 'loadouts.$[].itemsIds': itemId } }
    )
}

Notes:
- Entity documents don't store their own session id, so the deleted item's
  id can't be scoped to a single session/character up front. This sweeps
  Session.entities, Character.entities, and every Character.loadouts[].itemsIds
  by id across the collection instead.
- Only wired up for item ("entities") deletes, not Effect/Perk deletes.

